{"ticker": "IRMD", "run": "IRMD_20260826_050037", "verdict": {"ticker": "IRMD", "price": 87.85, "date": "2026-08-26", "model": "deepseek-v4-flash", "samples_run": 3, "n_basis": 3, "iv_band_low": 44.2, "iv_band_high": 65.4, "median_iv": 50.0, "spread_pct": 48.0, "flags": [], "pack_revision": 3, "scheme": "band_direction_v1", "direction": "overvalued", "size_hint": "quarter", "mos_vs_median_pct": -43.1, "consensus_dir": "IRMD_20260826_050037", "arm": "cloud_api", "pack_source": "fresh", "research_brief_age_days": 9.7, "searxng_up": true}, "samples": [{"sample": 1, "iv": 65.4, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 398, "report": "# RS2 v2.0 Integrated Investment Analysis \u2014 IRMD (iRadimed Corporation)\n\nT0 valuation date: **2026-08-24 (pack) / 2026-08-21 (macro retrieval)**  \nT0 price: **$87.85** [Tier 2 \u2014 vendor quote]  \nMarket cap: **$1.123B** | Shares out: **12,786,700** [Tier 2]\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 0 \u2014 ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\n| Item | Value / Tag |\n|---|---|\n| Enterprise archetype | **D \u2014 Product-Platform Hybrid** (hardware pump/monitor + recurring disposables) |\n| Valuation engine | **Engine 3 \u2014 Hybrid (Core Anchor + Platform Premium)** |\n| Intrinsic value (base) | **$65.40/share** (50% CI: $48\u2013$93; 80% CI: $39\u2013$118) |\n| Scenario-expected value | **$68.50/share** |\n| Margin of safety vs. $87.85 | **\u201328.1%** (none) |\n| Conviction | **8/15 \u2014 Medium** |\n| Final opinion | **HOLD / DO NOT INITIATE** \u2014 high-quality niche franchise, but price already discounts the bull path |\n\n**Engine selection rationale:**\n1. The company sells durable hardware (pumps, monitors, FMD) with a substantial installed base (**13,098 pump channels; 3,397 monitors sold** [Actual \u2014 FY2025 10-K]) that generates **recurring disposables + service revenue** (~35\u201340% of revenue [Estimate]).\n2. It is not a stable incumbent (growth 10\u201320%) and not a high-beta option story (positive FCF every year since 2018 [Actual \u2014 SEC companyfacts]).\n3. It is not a pure cyclical (zero debt, 76% gross margin, regulatory barrier) \u2014 though the 3860\u21923870 replacement cycle creates periodicity.\n4. Alternative engines would distort: Engine 1 (DCF alone) under-weights the platform attach (disposables + DERS drug library software). Engine 4 (expectation-driven) over-weights optionality for a business already generating cash. **Engine 3** captures the hybrid by separating core hardware value from recurring-platform premium.\n5. **Transition trigger check:** Not in transition (no archetype shift). The 3870 is a product refresh, not a business model pivot \u2014 revenue still >50% hardware, but recurring attach is expanding (disposables +14% YoY in Q2-26 [Actual \u2014 transcript]).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1 \u2014 MACRO CONTEXT\n\n### 1-1. Macro variable matrix\n\n| Variable | Level / Direction | Source / Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| 10Y Treasury | **4.71%**, stable-to-up (0.04pt MoM; 0.44pt YoY) | [Actual \u2014 TradingEconomics/Fed H.15, 2026-08-21] |\n| Real rates | ~2.0% (10Y\u2013breakeven) | [Estimate] |\n| DXY | Elevated, stable | [Estimate \u2014 no direct retrieval; qualitative] |\n| Fed stance | **Neutral\u2011hold** \u2014 target range 3.50\u20133.75% (July 2026 FOMC minutes) | [Actual \u2014 Federal Reserve] |\n| Liquidity | Neutral; fed funds futures imply slow easing | [Estimate] |\n| Cycle position | Late expansion | [Estimate] |\n| Inflation | ~2.6\u20132.8%, still above target | [Estimate] |\n| Credit spreads | Tight | [Estimate] |\n\n### 1-2. Regime distribution\n\n| Regime | Probability |\n|---|---|\n| Goldilocks (low rates + growth) | 25% |\n| Reflation (high rates + growth) | 30% |\n| Stagflation (high rates + low growth) | 25% |\n| Recession (low rates + low growth) | 20% |\n\n### 1-3. Sensitivity (-3 to +3)\n\n| Axis | Score |\n|---|---|\n| Interest rates | -1 (capital-deferrable but disposables stick with installed base) |\n| Dollar | -2 (18% international revenue; weak intl growth already flagged [Estimate \u2014 research brief]) |\n| Liquidity | +1 (niche, low beta) |\n| Economic cycle | -1 (MRI essential, but capital purchases deferrable) |\n| Commodities | +1 (pass-through) |\n\n### 1-4. Macro alignment \u2014 **Mild headwind** (\u22120.5 conviction). Expected impact = 0.3\u00d7(\u20130.5) + 0.2\u00d7(\u20131.0) + 0.3\u00d7(\u20130.75) \u2248 **\u22120.6\u03c3** [Estimate]. Intrinsic value unchanged; position sizing/entry discipline tightened.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1.5 \u2014 BASE RATE CHECK\n\n| Base-rate question | Rate | Versus IRMD |\n|---|---|---|\n| Profitable niche device co. alive in 5y | ~80% [Estimate] | 90%+ \u2014 profitable 8 of last 9 years, net cash [Actual] |\n| Platform transition success (3860\u21923870) | ~55\u201370% [Estimate] | 70\u201375% \u2014 installed-base pull, bookings 2\u00d7 shipments [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 call] |\n| TAM narrative fully achieved (40% share of $585M market by 2031) | ~15\u201325% [Estimate] | Bull case only |\n| Large-cap enter niche (Baxter/ICU/B. Braun develop 510(k) non-magnetic pump) | ~30% [Estimate] | Risk case: 25\u201335% over 5y |\n\n**Deviation from base rate:** Base case already assumes management\u2019s replacement-cycle story (1,000 channels/yr of the 6,400-channel pool [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 call]) plus sustained greenfield share gain. That is **not** a 1.5\u00d7+ deviation; it maps to a mid-base-rate outcome. No red-flag re-evaluation required.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2 \u2014 BUSINESS QUALITY\n\n### 2-1. Business understanding\n*3-sentence summary:* IRMD designs and sells non-magnetic, MRI-compatible IV infusion pumps (3860/3870 series) and patient monitors, plus ferro-magnetic detection systems, to hospitals. Once hardware is installed, it monetizes through proprietary disposables, DERS drug-library software, and service contracts. Its dominance of the \"pump inside the MRI suite\" workflow is protected by 510(k) clearance and the clinical cost