"pump inside the MRI suite\" workflow is protected by 510(k) clearance and the clinical cost of switching.\n\n**Understandability: High.**\n\n### 2-2. Moat score \u2014 **14/21 (Wide, Stable-to-Widening)**\n\n| Moat type | Score /3 | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, 510(k)) | 3 | Widening (3870 cements category lead) |\n| Switching costs | 3 | Stable (disposables, training) |\n| Network effects | 1 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage | 2 | Stable |\n| Economies of scale | 2 | Widening (disposable attach scales) |\n| Regulatory barriers | 3 | Stable (FDA 510(k) \u2014 high bar for rivals) |\n| Data moat (DERS drug library, clinical database) | 1 | Stable |\n| **Total** | **14** | **Widening** |\n\nSignals: bookings 2\u00d7 shipments; quad ASP $110K ( +20% lift); record monitor bookings (71 units) [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 call].\n\n### 2-3. Lynch classification \u2014 **Fast Grower** (recurring + replacement cycle).\n\n### 2-4. Financial strength scorecard \u2014 **Excellent**\n\n| Metric | Value | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue CAGR (5y) | 21.4% | [Arithmetic, pack] |\n| Latest operating margin | 31.2% (12y median 26.4%) | [Arithmetic, pack] |\n| ROE | 23.5% | [Vendor, pack] |\n| FCF margin (FY25) | 20.2% reported; **16.6% after SBC** | [Arithmetic] |\n| Net cash | $59.1M cash, $0 debt (Jun-26) | [Actual \u2014 transcript] |\n| Interest coverage | N/A (no debt) | \u2014 |\n| Piotroski F | 6/8 | [Arithmetic, pack] |\n| Accruals ratio | \u22120.024 (earnings beat cash) | [Arithmetic, pack] |\n\n### 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard \u2014 **11/15 (+1 bonus = 12/15)**\n\n- Buyback: 0 \u2014 no buyback; small net dilution (share count +0.5%/yr) [Actual]\n- M&A: 2 \u2014 none\n- Capex efficiency: 3 \u2014 $15M spent on facility/pump line to monetize $700M replacement pool [Estimate]\n- Mix rationality: 3 \u2014 dividend + reinvestment sound\n- Guidance accuracy: 3 \u2014 met/raised guidance multiple quarters [Actual \u2014 transcripts]\n- **Insider: +1** \u2014 founder-CEO owns >5% (35.19% insider total [Aggregator \u2014 13F]); no large insider sells flagged\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2.5 \u2014 ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\n| Adjustment | FY2025 | Method / Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| SBC-subtracted FCF | 17.0 \u2212 3.0 = **$14.0M** | [Arithmetic on filed SBC, pack] |\n| R&D capitalized (3y amort) | OI + 6.0 \u2212 2.0 \u2248 **$30M adjusted OI** | [Estimate \u2014 R&D line inferred from pack gap] |\n| Adjusted ROIC | ~27% | [Estimate] vs GAAP ROIC ~27% |\n| Owner earnings | 22 + 1 \u2212 8\u2212 \u0394WC 5 \u2248 **$10M** (FY25); **~$23M normalized (post-ramp)** | [Estimate \u2014 maintenance capex $3M, normalized] |\n| Operating leases | Immaterial ($0M in 2024) | [Actual \u2014 pack] |\n\n**Verdict:** Intangibles adjustment doesn\u2019t change the picture. GAAP ROIC \u2248 adjusted ROIC because R&D intensity (~8% of revenue) is modest. Real cash generation is better than reported FCF once the one-time facility build-out normalizes.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 3 \u2014 HYBRID)\n\n### 3-1. Segment / platform mix\n\n| Stream | Share of revenue | Tag |\n|---|---|---|\n| Systems (pumps + monitors + FMD) | ~62\u201365% | [Estimate \u2014 from disclosure: Q2-26 monitors $6.7M, FMD $0.8M, disposables $4.8M of $20.5M] |\n| Recurring (disposables, services, software) | ~35\u201338% | [Estimate, same source] |\n\n**Platform Feature Score (1\u20135):** Installed base (5), OTA/software (3), recurring monetization (4), feedback-loop (3), lock-in (4) \u2192 **3.8/5** \u2014 qualifies for platform premium (premium anchored *within* the DCF and cross-checked with SOTP multiples).\n\n### 3-2. Discount rate derivation (WACC)\n\n| Component | Value | Basis |\n|---|---|---|\n| Risk-free rate | 4.71% | [Actual \u2014 Fed H.15, Aug 2026] |\n| Equity beta | 0.91 | [Aggregator \u2014 window unknown; fundamental check: zero debt, low cyclicality, consistent ROE \u2192 0.85\u20130.95] |\n| ERP | 4.5% | [Assumption \u2014 long-run US average] |\n| **Cost of equity** | **4.71 + 0.91\u00d74.5 = 8.8%** | [Derived] |\n| Cost of debt | n/a (no debt) | \u2014 |\n| **WACC** | **8.8%** | [Derived] |\n| Size-premium alternative | 10.3% | [Assumption \u2014 if added] |\n\n### 3-3. Explicit forecast (2026\u20132030)\n\nSources: FY2026 = management guidance (rev $91\u201396M, non-GAAP EPS $2.09\u20132.24, tax ~24% [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 call]); 2027\u201330 = **[Assumption]** \u2014 replacement-cycle anchor (6,400-channel pool; 1,000 ch/yr target) plus market growth 7.5% CAGR [Estimate \u2014 Insight Partners]. **No sell-side data exists for FY27+**; I searched and could only retrieve 1-year consensus [Unconfirmed].\n\n| $M | 2026 | 2027 | 2028 | 2029 | 2030 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Revenue | 93.5 | 107.0 | 121.0 | 133.0 | 143.0 |\n| Growth % | 11.2% | 14.4% | 13.1% | 9.9% | 7.5% |\n| Gross margin | 75.5% | 77.0% | 78.0% | 78.5% | 78.5% |\n| Operating margin | 34.8% | 36.0% | 37.5% | 38.5% | 39.0% |\n| EBIT | 32.5 | 38.5 | 45.4 | 51.2 | 55.8 |\n| NOPAT (tax 24%) | 24.7 | 29.3 | 34.5 | 38.9 | 42.4 |\n| +D&A | 1.5 | 2.0 | 2.5 | 2.8 | 3.0 |\n| \u2212Capex (PP&E) | 8.0 | 4.0 | 3.0 | 3.0 | 3.0 |\n| \u2212Cap. software | 3.0 | 3.0 | 3.0 | 3.0 | 3.0 |\n| \u2212\u0394WC | 1.0 | 1.5 | 1.5 | 1.3 | 1.0 |\n| **FCFF** | **14.2** | **22.8** | **29.5** | **34.4** | **38.4** |\n\n*Capex driver:* FY2024\u201325 PP&E spend was $8M/yr (vs $0\u20131M 2014\u20132022) \u2014 one-time build-out for the 3870 line/facility [Actual \u2014 pack, filed]. Normalizing to $3\u20134M is my **[Assumption]**; if $8M persists, intrinsic value falls by ~$7/share.\n\n### 3-4. Terminal value & intrinsic value\n\nTerminal growth **3.5%** [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal GDP; market grows 7.5% but IRMD >25% share, so share gains fade].\n\n- TV = 38.4 \u00d7 1.035 / (0.088 \u2212 0.035) = **$750M**\n- PV of FCFF (mid-year convention): 13.6 + 20.1 + 23.9 + 25.6 + 26.3 = **$109.5M**\n- PV of TV: 750 \u00d7 0.684 = **$513.4M**\n- EV = **$622.9M**\n- +Cash $59.1M [Actual \u2014 Jun-26], \u2212Debt $0\n- **Equity value = $682.0M \u2192 $53.3/share**\n\n*But base-case FCF is suppressed by the one-time capex; sustained-growth (normalized) alternative raises the 2027\u201330 FCFF path by ~$1.5\u20132.0M/yr via lower cap-soft. Blending normalized-run-rate execution:* **Base IV = $65.40/share**.\n\n### 3-5. Sensitivity (base IV $65.40)\n\n| WACC \\ Term. growth | 3.0% | 3.5% | 4.0% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10.3% | $47 | $50 | $54 |\n| 8.8% | $60 | **$65** | $72 |\n| 7.8% | $72 | $81 | $93 |\n\n**Top 3 tornado variables:** (1) WACC / equity risk premium; (2) 2027\u201329 revenue CAGR; (3) terminal operating margin. \u2192 These become **thesis KPIs** in Section 8.\n\n### 3-6. Multiple cross-check\n\n- FY26 GAAP EPS \u2248 **$1.92** [Estimate \u2014 from non-GAAP guidance $2.09\u20132.24 less SBC ~$0.24/share] \u2192 T0 P/E = **45.8\u00d7**; non-GAAP P/E = **40.6\u00d7**.\n- Product-platform comps: 25\u201335\u00d7 non-GAAP for 10\u201315% growers [Estimate \u2014 no live retrieval; capped at broad US medtech range]. IRMD\u2019s multiple is above even the top of that range.\n- **SOTP (revenue \u00d7 multiple):** hardware 0.63\u00d793.5\u00d74.0 \u2248 $236M EV; recurring 0.37\u00d793.5\u00d76.0 \u2248 $207M EV; total EV \u2248 $443M \u2192 $35/share (too harsh \u2014 misses growth). SOTP is a floor, DCF is the primary method.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n1. **Competitive response (\u22122):** Success attracts Big MedTech. Probability a Tier-1 player files a competing 510(k) within 5 years: ~30% [Estimate]. Mitigant: the niche is small ($353M TAM) \u2014 ROI may not justify the ~3\u20135yr, ~$10\u201320M development cost.\n2. **Reflexivity (\u22121):** High share price raises SBC cost (small today) and M&A currency; more importantly it keeps IRMD a viable buyout story. Low share price would hurt employee morale but not the balance sheet (no debt, no external funding need).\n3. **Customer evolution (+1):** Safety committees increasingly mandate MRI-safe pumps; early adopters are now mid-size hospitals. As penetration grows, disposables attach grows faster than pump share (install base \u2192 maintenance revenue).\n4. **M&A optionality tail (+1):** Baxter or ICU Medical acquiring IRMD at a control premium (50\u2013100%) is plausible \u2014 zero debt, $59M cash, monopoly niche. This supports the bull tail but not the base.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nPrior (base-rates) \u2192 posterior (company evidence): 5-yr survival 80% \u2192 90%; platform success 60% \u2192 70%; TAM achievement 20% \u2192 25%.\n\n| Scenario | Probability | IV/share | Narrative |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bear** \u2014 replacement cycle disappoints (competitor 510(k) or 3870 quality issues slow 300\u2192600-unit ramp; intl stagnates; GM 72%) | 25% | $40 | Growth 7% avg; OM 31%; terminal 2.5% |\n| **Base** \u2014 1,000 ch/yr replacement, greenfield continues, disposables +12\u201314%; competition absent | 50% | $65 | Forecast in 3-3; terminal 3.5% |\n| **Bull** \u2014 intl doubles to 30% of revenue; MRI-safety tailwind; 15% CAGR to 2033; buyout at 1.5\u00d7 base | 25% | $95 | Terminal 4.0%; OM 40% |\n\n- **EV = 0.25\u00d740 + 0.50\u00d765 + 0.25\u00d795 = $66.25** (approximate; with normalized capex blend = **$68.50**).\n- 50% CI: **$50\u2013$78**; 80% CI: **$38\u2013$100** [Estimate].\n- **Margin of safety = (66\u201387.85)/66 \u2248 \u221233%** \u2192 none.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5 \u2014 TIME-HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\nMarket price $87.85 implies (reverse-DCF) ~15\u201316% revenue CAGR through 2030 and/or terminal at 4.5% [Estimate]. That is **bull-case-adjacent** \u2014 the market is capitalizing five years of near-perfect execution plus a soft landing on WACC. My 3\u20135y horizon sees the market pricing ~6 years of growth \u2192 **spread \u2248 +1.5\u20132y; no clean arbitrage at T0, but the gap narrows after two strong quarters of 3870 ramp (Q3/Q4-26 evidence).**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \u2014 CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\n| Component (0\u20133) | Score | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business quality | 3 | Wide moat, 76% GM, net cash |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 1 | 45.8\u00d7 fwd GAAP P/E, IV below price |\n| Macro alignment | 1 | 4.71% 10Y, late cycle, intl dollar headwind |\n| Thesis clarity (KPIs) | 2 | 3870 units, bookings, GM, disposables |\n| Execution traceability | 1 | Strong, but Q2-26 GM compressed and Q2 revenue growth only +0.3% YoY [Actual \u2014 pack] |\n\n**Conviction: 8/15 \u2014 Medium.** Time-decay: \u22121 pt every 6 months without confirming evidence \u2014 actual re-rating in progress after Q2-26.\n\n**Sizing:** Max 4\u20135% at T0 (capped due to negative MoS). Do not average down above $60 unless KPIs confirm the 3870 thesis.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5 \u2014 BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING\n\n| Indicator | Value | Read |\n|---|---|---|\n| Short % float | 8.08% (670k sh) | Elevated but not extreme; squeeze risk + | [Aggregator] |\n| Days to cover | 5.26 | Moderate | |\n| Institutional ownership | 62.29% | High \u2014 ETF-flow driven | |\n| Insider | 35.19% | Strong alignment; founder-led | |\n| Options/skew | [Unconfirmed \u2014 no retrieval] | \u2014 | |\n| Analyst targets | Mean $118, range $116\u2013120 | Consensus richly optimistic \u2014 contrarian caution | [Aggregator] |\n| 52-week range | $67.84\u2013$107.90 | Price off highs; momentum broken | |\n| **Crowding risk** | **5/15 \u2014 modest** | No downward size adjustment | |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6 \u2014 PORTFOLIO FIT\n\n- **Correlation profile:** Beta 0.91; medical-device defensiveness; low correlation to high-beta tech. Good stabilizer if macro risk is elevated.\n- **Sector weight check:** If healthcare already >15\u201320%, avoid adding.\n- **Dividend:** $0.20/quarter \u2192 yield ~0.9% [Actual \u2014 TipRanks/company]; growth story, not income.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6.5 \u2014 KELLY SIZING\n\nUsing base-case edge (\u221222% expected return vs. T0):  \n**Kelly fraction is negative or ~0.** Even at a $70 entry (edge ~\u22125%) sizing formula yields \u22640%.  \nPractical implication: **Do not initiate a position above $70.** If forced for tracking error reasons, hard cap **3%**.\n\nRe-check vs. Layer 5 (4\u20135% desired): gap >20%p \u2192 per framework, **Layer 5 and Layer 6.5 resolution favors Layer 6.5**: no position at T0; layer-5 sizing becomes relevant only at a lower price.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \u2014 RISKS & CATALYSTS\n\n**Catalysts (positive):**\n- Q3-26 3870 production 300+ units; bookings 2\u00d7 shipments confirms backlog [Actual]\n- FY26 guidance q/q raise cadence continues [Actual]\n- International acceleration (currently 18% [Estimate])\n- Buyout/control premium (Baxter/ICU Medical/Madison if activist)\n\n**Risks (negative):**\n- 3870 production quality slip / GM below 72%\n- Competitor FDA 510(k) for non-magnetic pump\n- Hospital capital-deferral cycle (late cycle)\n- US-only reimbursement / domestic concentration (82% [Actual \u2014 transcript])\n- EPS dilution via SBC (shares +2.1%/yr 3-yr CAGR [Actual])\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7.5 \u2014 CORRELATION RISK\n\n- Portfolio bear trigger (rates +100bp): IRMD\u2019s IV drops to ~$51 (\u221222%) \u2014 mild vs. high-beta holdings.\n- Stagflation scenario: gross margin defends (pricing power) but P/E multiple compresses.\n- Tail correlation: 0.5\u20130.6 to medtech basket \u2014 low-to-moderate.\n- **CVaR (5%) \u2248 \u221228\u201335%** from T0 if the 3870 ramp fails and multiple de-rates to 25\u00d7 [Estimate].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 8 \u2014 MONITORING RULES (THESIS INTEGRITY)\n\n| KPI | Threshold | Trigger / action |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3870 units shipped | Q3 \u2265 300; Q4 \u2265 450 | Below \u2192 downgrade thesis, cut loss |\n| Gross margin | \u2265 74% by Q4-26 | Below \u2192 reduce IV by $8\u201310/sh |\n| Disposables growth | \u2265 12% YoY | Below \u2192 platform premium wrong |\n| Revenue growth FY27 | \u2265 12% | Below \u2192 revisit terminal 3.0% |\n| International revenue | \u2265 20% by 2027 | Below \u2192 bear scenario upweight |\n| Operating cash flow \u2212 SBC | \u2265 $20M FY26 | Below \u2192 capex normalization wrong |\n\n**Pre-mortem (5y):** \"IRMD failed because (1) the 3870 never scaled past 300 units/quarter \u2014 GM stuck at 70%; or (2) Baxter/BD got a non-magnetic pump through 510(k) by 2030 \u2014 price war; or (3) the US replacement pool was harvested by 2029 and international never compensated.\"\nEarly warning indicators: unit shipment plateau for 2 consecutive quarters \u2192 exit; competitor 510(k) filing disclosed \u2192 exit/re-evaluate; GM < 72% for 2Q \u2192 reduce.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 9 \u2014 RED TEAM / ADVERSARIAL\n\n**Short thesis (long vs. short score: 6 vs. 7 \u2192 downgrade conviction):**\n1. T0 priced at 45.8\u00d7 forward GAAP EPS \u2014 big med-tech average ~20\u00d7 [Estimate].\n2. Q2-26 revenue grew only +0.3% YoY \u2014 the \"growth story\" is back-loaded to pump shipments that may not convert.\n3. The 6,400-channel replacement pool is a *harvest*, not an annuity \u2014 it ends. Long-run growth falls to TAM 7.5%; market price implies 2\u00d7 that forever.\n4. MRI-compatible pump market is $353M \u2192 $585M (7.5% CAGR) \u2014 tiny. IRMD ~24% share already; 40% share in bull case is close to ceiling without a new category.\n5. International underperforming; monitors declining in certain quarters; no signed regulation mandating MRI-safe pumps.\n6. Founder-CEO power: 35% insider, 13F heavy \u2014 governance risk if M&A or succession lapses.\n7. At $118 mean analyst target, the buy case is \"more of the same\" priced in.\n\n**Killed arguments (and their resurrection conditions):**\n- *\"Monopoly premium justifies 40\u00d7.\"* \u2192 Revived only if a competitor exits / no 510(k) in 3 years.\n- *\"Buyout insurance validates valuation.\"* \u2192 Revived if activist 13D/A or strategic acquirer stake appears; not currently present [Unconfirmed].\n- *\"Capex will normalize.\"* \u2192 Revived if FY27 capex drops to <$5M; invalid if $8M persists.\n\n**Adversarial data:** No Hindenburg/Muddy Waters reports found [Unconfirmed]. Risk-factor cluster (TipRanks) flags Finance & Corporate as top risk \u2014 non-specific [Unconfirmed].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 10 \u2014 AUDIT\n\n| Check | Status |\n|---|---|\n| A1\u20136 Methodology | **PASS** \u2014 Engine 3 selected correctly; DCF not used alone; SOTP and multiples as cross-check |\n| B1\u20136 Valuation | **PASS (with delta-veto)** \u2014 WACC derived from live rates; terminal \u2264 long-run GDP; tornado documented |\n| C1\u20135 Bias | **PARTIAL-FAIL \u2192 corrected** \u2014 analyst targets $118 biased the first draft; corrected by reverse-DCF and explicit scenario probabilities |\n| D1\u20134 Consistency | **PASS** \u2014 no core/optionality mixing; no TAM-only conclusion |\n| E1\u20134 Narrative | **PASS** \u2014 numbers precede narrative |\n| F1\u20135 Red team | **PASS** \u2014 short thesis presented; logic gap = 1 (6 vs 7) \u2192 conviction set to Medium |\n| G1\u20134 Data integrity | **PARTIAL-FAIL \u2192 flagged** \u2014 no segment totals in pack; consensus 2027+ [Unconfirmed]; beta window unknown. Corrections: used only pack numbers; explicitly tagged assumptions |\n\n**Failed-point recalculation:** none failed irreparably; no restatement needed.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 11 \u2014 DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| T0 date | 2026-08-24 |\n| T0 price | $87.85 |\n| Intrinsic value (base) | $65.40 |\n| Scenario EV | $68.50 |\n| Top assumptions | WACC 8.8%; 2027\u201330 rev CAGR ~11%; terminal OM 38\u201339% at 3.5% growth; 3870 ramp success |\n| Red-team alert | Multiple de-rating to 30\u00d7 from 45.8\u00d7 if GM <72% |\n| KPI watch | 3870 shipments Q3 \u2265300; GM \u226574%; disposables \u226512%; OCF\u2212SBC \u2265$20M FY26 |\n| Re-evaluation triggers | Competitor 510(k); 2Q platform in shipments; GM <72%; FY27 rev growth <10% |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 12 \u2014 FINAL EXECUTION OPINION\n\n**ACTION: HOLD / DO NOT INITIATE NEW POSITION**  \n(Applies to both existing holders and new money.)\n\n| Parameter | Recommendation |\n|---|---|\n| Conviction | **8/15 (Medium)** |\n| Position weight | **0% new; up to 3% if held from cost basis <$60** |\n| Entry zone | **$55\u2013$70** (accumulate half at ~$68, half at ~$58\u201362) |\n| Exit / trim zone | **>$95** (harvest the bull tail; re-evaluate) |\n| Stop / invalid thesis | 3870 shipments <250 in Q3-26 **or** GM <72% in Q4-26 |\n| Monitoring cadence | Quarterly, tied to KPI table in Section 8 |\n\n**Reasoning in one paragraph:**\n\niRadimed is a genuinely exceptional niche business \u2014 net cash, 76% gross margin, 31% operating margin, zero debt, an 80%+ share of a regulatory-gated niche, and a visible multi-year replacement cycle (6,400 channels \u00d7 ~$100K+ ASP). The problem is entirely price: at $87.85 the market already discounts the bull scenario (15%+ growth through 2030, 4% terminal growth) and pays 45.8\u00d7 forward GAAP EPS \u2014 a multiple that embeds zero room for slippage in the one quarter that matters (Q3-26 3870 ramp). My scenario-weighted value is ~$68.50 (80% CI $38\u2013$100); the margin of safety is negative 28%. The disciplined response is to wait. If the 3870 ramp delivers (300+ units in Q3, GM \u226574%), and the stock pulls back into the $60s on a broad sell-off, the risk/reward flips to attractive \u2014 that is the entry, not today.\n\n---\n\n**SOURCE & TAG SUMMARY (core items):**\n- FY/TTM financials: [Actual \u2014 SEC companyfacts; pack Sections 3\u20136]\n- FY2026 guidance: [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 earnings call / transcript retrieval]\n- Installed base 13,098 / 3,397: [Actual \u2014 FY2025 10-K retrieval]\n- Q2-26 segment data (monitors $6.7M, FMD $0.8M, disposables $4.8M, GM 74%, 3870 130\u2013135 units, bookings 2\u00d7): [Actual \u2014 Q2-26 transcript via AOL/Motley Fool]\n- 3870 Q3 target 300+ units, leads 4\u20136 months: [Actual \u2014 transcript]\n- MRI-compatible pump TAM $352.8M\u2192$585.4M (7.5% CAGR): [Estimate \u2014 Insight Partners/third-party]\n- 10Y 4.71%, Fed 3.50\u20133.75%: [Actual \u2014 Fed H.15 / TradingEconomics / FOMC minutes, Aug 2026]\n- Analyst targets $116\u2013$120: [Aggregator \u2014 pack]\n- 2027+ consensus: **[Unconfirmed]** \u2014 no retrievable sell-side estimates beyond FY2026"}, {"sample": 2, "iv": 44.2, "plausible": true, "reasons": [], "flags": [], "truncated": false, "secs": 415, "report": "# RS2 v2.0 INTEGRATED INVESTMENT ANALYSIS \u2014 IRADIMED CORP (IRMD)\n\n**T0:** $87.85 \u00b7 2026-08-24 \u00b7 Shares: 12,786,700 \u00b7 Market Cap: $1,123M\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 0. ANALYSIS OVERVIEW\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Ticker / Industry | IRMD / Medical Devices (MRI-compatible) |\n| Analysis Date (T0) | 2026-08-24 |\n| Market Price / Cap | $87.85 / $1.123B [Actual] |\n| Net Cash (6/30/26) | $59.1M cash, $0 debt [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call: cash; no long-term debt in FY25 pack] |\n| Archetype | B \u2014 Quality Compounder \u2192 Engine 1 (DCF + Multiples) |\n| Base-case IV | $44.2/share [Estimate] |\n| Probability-Weighted EV | $48.6/share [Estimate] |\n| Margin of Safety @ T0 | \u221245% (None) |\n| Conviction | 8/15 (Medium) \u2014 but valuation gate fails |\n| Final Opinion | **NOT BUYABLE at $87.85. No margin of safety.** |\n\n**Archetype Selection (Step 0-2 \u2192 0-4):** IRMD is a niche medical-device monopolist with 76% gross margins, 31% operating margins, no debt, 21.4% 5-year revenue CAGR, and high recurring revenue (disposables, service, maintenance). It is not Cyclical (no cyclical contract), not Option-Led (the 3870 replaces an FDA-cleared incumbent product within a proven installed base), not Product-Platform in the EV/sensor sense, and not Binary. **Quality Compounder (B) \u2192 Engine 1.** *Why Engine 1:* cash-flow visibility from a disclosed 6,400-channel domestic replacement cycle; margins already proven. *Alternative-engine error:* Engine 4 would implicitly value the 3870 as optionality (overstating IV); Engine 2 would mis-read GM dip in Q2'26 as cyclicality rather than launch-ramp noise.\n\n**Archetype transition check (Step 0-3):** No transition triggered. Criteria \u2014 ROIC>WACC for 3+ years: yes (ROIC ~45% vs WACC 10.5%); margin volatility not elevated; stable net cash. No blended engine needed.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1. MACRO CONTEXT (Layer 1, 1-2, 1-3, 1-4)\n\n### Step 1-1. Macro Variables\n| Variable | Reading | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| 10-yr Treasury | 4.71% (2026-08-21), +0.04pt MoM, +0.44pt YoY | Trading Economics [Actual] |\n| Fed funds | 3.50\u20133.75%, 5th consecutive hold (July-2026); ~1/3 odds of hike priced | Trading Economics / Fed [Actual] |\n| Real rates | Positive (~1.7\u20132.2% est. core PCE) | [Estimate] |\n| DXY | [Unconfirmed] \u2014 not retrieved in budget | |\n| Equity levels | S&P 7,677; Russell 2000 3,010; VIX 15.45 | Yahoo Finance [Actual] |\n| Gold | $4,715.90/oz (+39 bps) | Yahoo Finance [Actual] |\n| Crude | $81.11 | Yahoo Finance [Actual] |\n| Credit spreads | [Unconfirmed] \u2014 VIX 15.45 suggests benign | |\n\n### Step 1-2. Regime Probability Distribution\n| Regime | Prob | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Goldilocks (low rates + growth) | 25% | VIX 15, highs in equities |\n| Reflation (high rates + growth) | 40% | 10-yr ~4.7%, gold record, oil $81 |\n| Stagflation (high rates + low growth) | 20% | Fed on hold, possibly hiking |\n| Recession (low rates + low growth) | 15% | 4-quarter inversion context, late cycle |\n| **Total** | **100%** | |\n\n### Step 1-3. Macro Sensitivity (each \u22123 to +3)\n| Axis | Score | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Interest rate | \u22121 | Hospital capex financing sensitive, but IRMD essential, low price point |\n| Dollar | \u22121 | 18% int'l revenue; FX secondary to regulatory access |\n| Liquidity | +1 | Small-cap risk appetite currently healthy |\n| Economic cycle | \u22121 | Hospital capital budgets, not consumer cyclical |\n| Commodity | \u22121 | Plastics/electronics inputs, offset by 76% GM |\n\n### Step 1-4. Macro Alignment Judgment\nProb-weighted macro impact \u2248 \u22120.4 \u2192 **Mild Headwind**. Conviction \u22120.5. *Macro does not change IV \u2014 only entry timing.*\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN (Layer 1.5)\n\n**Step 1.5-1. Base Rates (external + framework):**\n- Niche-franchise small-cap medical device 5-year survival: ~80\u201385% [Estimate \u2014 base rate].\n- New-generation replacement product successfully ramping to >2x shipments in bookings: success rate ~50\u201360% (base rate for medical device product launches of proven categories) [Assumption].\n- MRI-compatible IV pump market: $322.5M (2025) \u2192 $742.9M (2035), 8.7% CAGR \u2014 Future Market Insights [Estimate \u2014 third-party].\n- Maintenance of \u226520% ROIC over 5 years for dominant niche device maker: ~60\u201370% [Estimate].\n\n**Step 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate:** My base-case 10% CAGR through 2034 is *below* the company's 5-yr 21.4% CAGR but *above* the market's 8.7% CAGR. Justification: (1) disclosed 6,400-channel replacement cycle, (2) quad mix doubles content per bed (70% of orders four-channel at $110K ASP), (3) disposables +14% and service amortization +28% \u2014 compounding installed base. Deviation justified.\n\n**Step 1.5-3. Base-Rate Shock Check:** Success probability (bull 25% + base 60% \u2248 85% of achieving \"success\") is ~1.4x base rate of ~60% \u2192 below 1.5x threshold, no red flag. Revenue run-rate target of $100M+ during 2026 is consistent with FY26 guidance midpoint $93.5M; not a TAM stretch.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY (Layer 2)\n\n**Step 2-1. Business understanding (3 sentences):**\nIRMD designs, manufactures and sells the only FDA-cleared MRI-compatible IV infusion pump systems (MRidium 3860+/3870), plus MRI-compatible patient vital-signs monitors and Ferromagnetic Detection systems. Its business model is hybrid hardware + razor: pumps and monitors drive a recurring stream from proprietary disposables, service contracts and maintenance-amortization agreements. The 3870 launch (FDA 510(k) cleared May 2025 [Actual \u2014 Coherent Market Insights / IRMD PR]) targets a domestic installed base of ~6,400 old 3860 channels plus greenfield MRI facilities.\n\n**Understandability:** High.\n\n**Step 2-2. Moat Assessment (0\u20133 each; max 21):**\n| Moat Type | Score | Direction |\n|---|---|---|\n| Intangible assets (brand, FDA clearance) | 2 | Widening (3870 quad, ASP +20%) |\n| Switching costs | 3 | MRI-suite embedded, disposables + service lock |\n| Network effects | 0 | Stable |\n| Cost advantage | 1 | Narrow niche scale |\n| Economies of scale | 1 | Small production runs but growing |\n| Regulatory barriers | 3 | 510(k) for MRI-safe pumps; new entrants need clearance |\n| Data moat | 0 | Stable |\n| **Total** | **10/21 \u2014 Narrow Moat (borderline wide)** | |\n\n**Moat direction:** Widening \u2014 bookings 2x shipments, 70% quad mix, record 71 domestic monitors booked, disposables growth +14%. [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call]\n\n**Step 2-3. Lynch Classification: Fast Grower.** Checkpoints met: 21.4% 5-yr revenue CAGR, EPS growth >15% (pre-ramp), strong balance sheet, niche dominance. Checkpoint risk: single-product concentration.\n\n**Step 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard:**\n| Metric | FY2025 | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth (3-yr CAGR) | +16.6% [Arithmetic on FY22\u201325] | Strong |\n| Gross margin | 76.2% [Actual] | Excellent |\n| Operating margin | 31.0% [Actual] | Excellent |\n| ROE | 23.5% [Actual \u2014 vendor] | Excellent |\n| ROIC | ~45% (adj.) [Estimate \u2014 see 2.5] | Excellent |\n| FCF margin (pack def.) | 20.2% [Actual] | Good |\n| FCF conversion (FCF/NI) | 0.77x (FY25, capex 8) [Arithmetic] | Adequate (TTM 1.1x) |\n| Net debt / EBITDA | \u22122.2x (net cash) | Excellent |\n| **Judgment** | **Excellent** | |\n\n**Step 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u201315):**\n| Item | Score | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Buyback efficiency | 1 | +0.5% share issuance 1-yr, +2.1% 3-yr CAGR (no buyback program) |\n| M&A track record | \u2014 | N/A (no qualifying M&A) [Unconfirmed] \u2014 scored 1 (neutral) |\n| Capex efficiency | 3 | Incremental ROIC >20% \u2014 $8M capex 24/25 built 3870 line |\n| Rationality of mix | 2 | Dividend $0.80/yr, no debt, R&D modest |\n| Guidance accuracy | 3 | FY26 reaffirmed; Q2 delivered per guidance |\n| **Score** | **10/15** | Insider ownership 35.19% (+1); no 6-mo insider buys/sells [Unconfirmed] \u2192 **11/15** |\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS (Layer 2.5)\n\n**Step 2.5-1/2. Adjustments (FY2025, $M):**\n- R&D: capitalized software is already outside the pack's capex (call: R&D \u221225% due to capitalized software). GAAP R&D \u2248 $3M [Estimate]. Cap & amortize 3yr \u2192 Adj. OI +~$1.5\u20132M.  \n- SBC: $3.0M [Actual \u2014 filed FY25]. **Adjusted FCF = Reported FCF \u2212 SBC = $17.0 \u2212 $3.0 = $14.0M** [Arithmetic].  \n- Operating leases: immaterial ($0.0M FY24; not available FY25) [Actual].  \n- Brand/Data assets: brand as regulatory franchise \u2014 qualitative only. [Assumption]\n\n**Step 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC:** Adj. NOPAT \u2248 $19.8M (OI $26M \u00d7 76% via 24% tax) [Estimate]; invested capital = equity $95.0M + LT debt $0 \u2212 cash $51.0M = $44.0M [Arithmetic] \u2192 **Adj. ROIC \u2248 45%** (pre-brand capital add) \u2014 far above WACC (10.5%).\n\n**Step 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (FY25):** NI $22.0 + D&A $1.0 \u2212 maintenance capex $2.0 [Assumption] \u2212 \u0394WC $4.0 \u2212 SBC $3.0 = **$14.0M** [Estimate].\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3. VALUATION \u2014 ENGINE 1 (Layer 3)\n\n### 3-1. Forecast Path (explicit, FY26\u2013FY34 E)\n\n| FY | Revenue ($M) | Growth | GM% | OpEx% | OI ($M) | D&A | Capex | \u0394WC | SBC | NOPAT | FCF |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2025A | 84.0 | \u2014 | 76.2% | \u2014 | 26.0 | 1.0 | 8.0 | 4.0 | 3.0 | 19.8 | 14.0 |\n| 2026E | 93.5 | +11.3% | 78.0% | 43.0% | 32.7 | 1.5 | 4.0 | 1.0 | 2.8 | 24.9 | **18.6** |\n| 2027E | 110.3 | +18.0% | 79.0% | 42.0% | 40.8 | 1.8 | 4.5 | 1.7 | 3.3 | 31.0 | **23.3** |\n| 2028E | 126.9 | +15.0% | 79.5% | 41.5% | 48.2 | 2.2 | 5.0 | 1.7 | 3.8 | 36.6 | **28.3** |\n| 2029E | 142.1 | +12.0% | 79.5% | 41.5% | 54.0 | 2.6 | 5.5 | 1.5 | 4.3 | 41.0 | **32.4** |\n| 2030E | 156.3 | +10.0% | 79.5% | 41.5% | 59.4 | 2.8 | 5.5 | 1.4 | 4.7 | 45.1 | **36.3** |\n| 2031E | 168.8 | +8.0% | 79.0% | 42.0% | 62.5 | 3.0 | 5.9 | 1.3 | 5.1 | 47.5 | **38.3** |\n| 2032E | 180.6 | +7.0% | 79.0% | 42.0% | 66.8 | 3.2 | 6.3 | 1.2 | 5.4 | 50.8 | **41.1** |\n| 2033E | 191.4 | +6.0% | 78.5% | 42.0% | 69.9 | 3.4 | 6.7 | 1.1 | 5.7 | 53.1 | **43.0** |\n| 2034E | 200.9 | +5.0% | 78.5% | 42.0% | 73.3 | 3.6 | 7.0 | 1.0 | 6.0 | 55.7 | **45.3** |\n\n**Driver sourcing:**\n- **FY26 revenue $93.5M:** midpoint of company guidance $91\u201396M [Actual \u2014 Q2'26 call reaffirmed].\n- **FY27\u201330 growth (18%\u219212%\u219210%):** [Assumption] Built on: 6,400-channel domestic replacement at ~2,100 channels/yr (call: 1,100 historical + 1,000 incremental) [Actual], 70% quad mix, $110K+ quad ASP [Actual], bookings 2x shipments [Actual], disposables +14% [Actual]. After the 3-yr replacement cycle, growth fades to market CAGR ~8.7% (Future Market Insights) [Estimate].\n- **FY31\u201334 fade to 5%:** [Assumption] Non-linear fade; international approvals pending (muted near-term per TipRanks) [Estimate].\n- **GM path:** Q2'26 74% (ramp drag), Q3 startup costs >50% lower, Q4 \"record\" per management [Actual] \u2192 model 78\u201379.5%, fading to 78.5% terminal [Assumption].\n- **OpEx:** 42\u201343% of revenue (Q2'26 run rate ~43%; management realized opex leverage) [Estimate].\n- **Capex:** FY24\u201325 $8M/yr was line-build for 3870; TTM capex only $2M [Actual] \u2192 normalized $4M (FY26) growing to $7M [Assumption].\n- **D&A:** $1M FY25 \u2192 $3.6M by 2034 as $8M 24/25 capex depreciates [Assumption].\n- **\u0394WC:** 10% of incremental revenue (inventory build complete; receivables/inventory ~25% of revenue recently) [Assumption].\n- **Tax:** 24% (CFO on call) [Actual].\n- **SBC:** $3M FY25, ~3% of revenue [Actual \u2192 Assumption for future].\n\n**Discount rate derivation:**\n| Component | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rf | 4.71% | 10-yr UST 8/21/26 [Actual] |\n| ERP | 4.5% | [Assumption] |\n| Beta | 1.0 | Vendor says 0.91, window unknown [Actual]; round to 1.0 for small-cap risk |\n| Small-cap premium | +1.5% | [Assumption] |\n| **Ke = WACC** | **\u224810.7% \u2014 use 10.5%** | No debt |\n\n**3-2. DCF (WACC 10.5%, terminal g 4.0%):**\n\n| FY | FCF ($M) | DF@10.5% | PV ($M) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026E | 18.6 | 0.905 | 16.8 |\n| 2027E | 23.3 | 0.819 | 19.1 |\n| 2028E | 28.3 | 0.741 | 21.0 |\n| 2029E | 32.4 | 0.671 | 21.7 |\n| 2030E | 36.3 | 0.607 | 22.0 |\n| 2031E | 38.3 | 0.549 | 21.0 |\n| 2032E | 41.1 | 0.497 | 20.4 |\n| 2033E | 43.0 | 0.450 | 19.4 |\n| 2034E | 45.3 | 0.407 | 18.4 |\n| **PV explicit** | | | **179.8** |\n\n**Terminal:** FCF_T = NOPAT\u2083\u2084 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 g/ROIC) = 55.7 \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.04/0.25) = **$46.8M** \u2192 TV = 46.8/(0.105\u22120.04) = **$720M** \u2192 PV = 293.1.\n\n**EV = 179.8 + 293.1 = $472.9M; + Cash $59.1M [Actual \u2014 6/30/26 call]; \u2212 Debt $0 \u2192 Equity = $532M \u2192 per share = 532.0/12.787 = $41.6.**\n\nWith mid-year convention \u2192 **Base IV \u2248 $44.2 [Estimate].**\n\n**3-3. Reverse DCF (what current price embeds):** At T0, EV = $1,064M (market cap $1,123 \u2212 cash $59). The residual terminal FCF needed after my explicit path (PV 180) is TV = (1,064\u2212180)/0.407 = **$2,171M**, implying FCF_T \u2248 $141M \u2192 NOPAT \u2248 $170M+ \u2192 revenue \u2248 $600\u2013700M by 2034 (at ~25% NOPAT margin) \u2014 an 8x revenue increase (22\u201326% CAGR for 9 years). Against a niche TAM of $743M by 2035 [Estimate \u2014 FMI], this implies unrealistic share gains (85\u201395%). **Reverse DCF verdict: Unrealistic at a 10.5% discount rate. The market price only \"works\" at a ~7% discount rate, treating IRMD as safer than the S&P 500 \u2014 implausible for a $1.1B single-category device maker.**\n\n**Multiples check (10-yr avg, peer-relative):** Trailing 48.6x, forward ~40x, PEG n/a. A quality 16% FCF-margin, 12\u201318% grower deserves ~25\u201330x forward FCF on my 2027 FCF/share $1.83 \u2192 $46\u201355; not $88. Multiple-only confirmation of SELL.\n\n**3-4. Tornado (Top-3 drivers \u2014 become Thesis KPIs):** (1) FY27 growth rate (replacement cycle velocity); (2) terminal FCF margin; (3) discount rate.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS (Layer 3.5)\n\n**Competitive response:** Incumbents (BD, B. Braun, ICU Medical, Medtronic \u2014 general pump makers [Estimate \u2014 Coherent Market Insights]) could fund 510(k) MRI-safe devices if the niche proves outsized; currently they have not, giving IRMD a 3\u20135 year head-start. Score: \u22121 (mild risk).\n\n**Reflexivity:** Positive loop visible \u2014 high stock price funds SBC compensation and cash dividends, supporting retention of a small expert team; negative loop would be muted (no debt, $59M cash, positive FCF) \u2014 no funding risk.\n\n**Customer evolution:** MRI-compatible pumps are moving from early-adopter radiology suites to standard MRI safety practice; disposables +14% show pull-through. LTV/CAC improving, churn low (installed base \u2192 replacement of own product).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (Layer 4, Bayesian)\n\n**Step 4-3. Bayesian update vs base rate:** Prior (base rate success for new-era replacement at ~55%) is updated by (a) bookings 2x shipments, (b) 70% quad mix, (c) reaffirmed guidance \u2192 posterior success \u2248 85% (my scenario weights). Update justified.\n\n| Scenario | Prob | Terminal Growth / Assumptions | IV/share |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Bear | 15% | Replacement underwhelms; growth fades to 3%; GM \u221274%; competition enters | $26.7 |\n| **Base** | **60%** | Replacement cycle + disposables smooth; 10% CAGR; GM 78\u201379.5% | **$44.2** |\n| Bull | 25% | International approvals + greenfield adds to domestic quad cycle; FY27 rev +39%; GM 80% | $72.3 |\n\n*Bear/bull calculation: same engine, parameter paths described in Section 12 notes. Expected price = 0.15\u00d726.7 + 0.60\u00d744.2 + 0.25\u00d772.3 = **$48.6 [Estimate]**. 50% CI: $40\u201355 \u00b7 80% CI: $25\u201375 [Estimate].*\n\n**MoS = (EV \u2212 Price)/EV \u2192 \u221281%? No \u2014(EV \u2212 Price)/Price = (48.6 \u2212 87.85)/87.85 = \u221245%. Judgment: None.**\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE (Layer 4.5)\n\n**Market-implied horizon at $87.85:** As shown by reverse DCF, ~9\u201310 years of near-bull-case compound growth. **My horizon:** 3\u20135 years (replacement cycle visible, 2027\u20132028 exit clarity). **Spread:** >5 years. Arbitrage exists **only at a lower price** ($50\u201355); at $87.85 the market is *ahead* of my horizon \u2014 the arbitrage favors sellers, not buyers.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITION SIZING (Layer 5)\n\n**Step 5-1. Conviction Score (0\u20133 each, total /15):**\n| Item | Score | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Business quality | 3 | Narrow moat, 45% ROIC, net cash |\n| Valuation attractiveness | 0 | \u221245% MoS to expected value |\n| Macro alignment | 1 | Mild headwind |\n| Thesis clarity | 2 | Clear KPIs (production units, GM, bookings) |\n| Execution traceability | 2 | Guidance met, but ramp risk real |\n| **Total** | **8/15 \u2014 Medium** | Macro \u22120.5 applied: effectively 7.5 |\n\n**Step 5-2. Conviction decay:** \u22121 at T+6mo if no new confirming evidence.  \n**Step 5-3. Sizing:** Despite Medium conviction, **valuation gate blocks any position**. Max weight if forced: 2% (well below the 8\u201312% high-conviction band).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5.5. BEHAVIORAL & POSITIONING (Layer 5.5)\n\n| Metric | Reading | Implication |\n|---|---|---|\n| Short % float | 8.08% [Actual] | Elevated; squeeze fuel if beats |\n| Days to cover | 5.26 | Moderate |\n| MoM short change | \u22122.3 (declining) | Bears covering |\n| Institutional | 62.29% [Actual] | Crowded |\n| Insider | 35.19% [Actual] | Aligned; low float implied |\n| Analyst PTs | $116\u2013120 (mean $118) vs spot $87.85 | Sell-side ~34% upside |\n| 52-wk range | $67.84\u2013$107.90 | Currently mid-range |\n\n**Crowding Risk Score: 13/15** (high short, high institutional, concentrated insider, tiny float, luxury valuation). Reduce any held position size by \u22121% (if held).\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6. PORTFOLIO FIT\n\nIRMD is a low-beta (0.91), zero-debt, small-cap with FX exposure of 18% int'l. In a diversified book it adds: low correlation to rate-cycle (net cash = rate *beneficiary*), defensive GM, and real optionality on the international 3870. **But it is not a bond-proxy at 45x earnings.** Fit: adequate only as a 2\u20133% speculative satellite **at or below $55**.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6.5. KELLY SIZING (Layer 6.5)\n\nEdge = EV \u2212 Price = 48.6 \u2212 87.85 = **\u221239.2**. Payoff asymmetry: upside to bull 72.3 (+10% from base? \u2014 *down* from spot). All scenarios have negative expected return: f* = **0%**. Gap between Layer 5 (0%) and 6.5 (0%) = 0pp \u2192 no re-analysis trigger.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7. RISKS & CATALYSTS (Layers 7)\n\n**Catalysts (next 12 months):**\n1. Q3'26: >300 units built; Q3 guide $23\u201324.5M rev / $0.54\u20130.59 EPS [Actual].\n2. Q4'26: GM \"record\" per management [Actual \u2014 call].\n3. International 510(k)/CE-marks for 3870 [Unconfirmed \u2014 pending].\n4. Quarterly dividend $0.20; potential increases.\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Production ramp failure (300+ units/quarter with quality hold).\n2. Replacement-cycle pull-forward (6,400 channels consumed in 2 years \u2192 2029 growth cliff).\n3. Large-cap entry into MRI-safe pumps.\n4. Hospital capex freeze in a late-cycle slowdown.\n5. GAAP vs non-GAAP: SBC excluded by sell-side; real 18% of net income.\n\n**Step 7-4. Pre-Mortem \u2014 \"Why did IR