                            1/3\nMOAT SCORE: 13/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT (lower end)\nMoat Direction: WIDENING near-term (quad conversion raises lock-in; 3870 ASP\n+20%; no direct competitor has filed 510(k) [Unconfirmed\u2014FDA database not\nsearched, but no public filing found in research]). STABLE-to-NARROWING\npost-cycle (TAM ceiling, potential me-too entrants by 2028\u20132030).\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification: STALWART trending FAST GROWER during the\nreplacement cycle (2027\u20132029), reverting to STALWART. Checkpoints:\n- Earnings growth fueled by unit volume + mix (quad), NOT financial leverage \u2713\n- Balance sheet: net cash $59.1M [Actual \u2014 call] \u2713\n- Durability of growth window: quantified (6,400 pool) \u2713\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard (FY2025 unless noted):\n- Revenue 3-yr CAGR (FY22\u2192FY25): +16.6% [Arithmetic]; last-4Q rev: $86.0M [Arithmetic]\n- Operating margin: 3-yr avg 28.7% [Arithmetic]; latest 31.2% [Arithmetic]\n- Net income growth (FY22\u2192FY25): $13M\u2192$22M, 19.2% CAGR [Arithmetic]\n- ROE: 23.5% [Aggregator]; ROIC \u2248 23% (no debt, equity $95M) [Estimate]\n- FCF margin: FY25 $17M/$84M = 20.2% [Arithmetic]; FCF conversion (FCF/NI) = 77%\n- Net debt: NET CASH $59.1M [Actual]; total debt $0 [Vendor; LT debt not filed for\n  IRMD in pack \u2014 treating as $0 debt is [Unconfirmed] but immaterial given cash]\n- Interest coverage: N/A (no debt)\nJudgment: EXCELLENT\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard (0\u20133 \u00d7 5):\n- Buyback efficiency:          0/3 (no buybacks; +0.5% share dilution/yr)\n- M&A track record:            0/3 (none \u2014 neutral, not destructive)\n- Capex efficiency:            2/3 (facility build FY23\u201325 $7\u20138M; revenue +$18M\n                                  FY22\u219225; incremental ROIC >30% [Estimate])\n- Rationality of mix:          2/3 (dividend $0.20/qtr \u2248 45% payout; no waste)\n- Guidance accuracy:           3/3 (FY26 raised; Q2 met; Q1 beat; history strong)\nS